'''battery-box''' (bat′ėr-i-boks), ''n.'' A square chest or box, filled with earth, used for making parapets for batteries where gabions or sand-bags are not to be had. ''Farrow'', Mil. Encyc.

'''battery-gun''' (bat′ėr-i-gun), ''n.'' A machine-gun (which see).

